.TH PATH_CANONICAL 3
.SH NAME
path_canonical \- canonicalize a path string
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <path.h>
.PP
.BI "int path_canonical(const char* " path ", stralloc* " out ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B path_canonical
takes a null-terminated string
.I path
and converts it into its canonical form, storing the result in the
.B stralloc
pointed to by
.IR out .
.PP
The conversion involves copying the input path into
.I out
and then invoking
.BR path_canonical_sa (3)
to perform in-place normalization, such as resolving "." and ".." components and collapsing redundant separators.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 1 on success, or 0 if an error occurred during canonicalization.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR path_canonical_sa (3),
.BR path_normalize (3),
.BR stralloc (3)